course: dictionary
lesson: 15899
title: Unload: taking things out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To unload means to take things off or out of a vehicle, machine or container. «Dad and I unload the shopping from the car» means we carry the bags out of the boot, so the car is empty afterwards.
explain: You can also unload a machine. «Mum asked me to unload the dishwasher» means take the clean plates out of it. The word tells you the thing is being emptied.
explain: Read the words around unload to check the meaning. «The lorry was unloaded at the port» has a clue in it: lorries carry goods, and at the port the goods come off. Now try a different idea: «Sam unloaded his worries onto his big sister.» Here it does not mean taking things out of a box. It means he told her about his worries, so they were no longer kept inside him.
fact: To unload means to take things off or out of a vehicle, machine or container.
fact: To unload a vehicle or machine means to empty it.
fact: Informally, to unload your worries means to tell someone about them.
fact: Ships and lorries are unloaded at ports.
fact: In maths problems, unloading boxes means subtracting them from the total.
exercise: «Dad and I unload the shopping from the car.» What does unload mean here? | To wash the car | To fill up with more things | *To take things out of the car | To drive the car away
exercise: Ella's family unload the dishwasher every evening. What does unloading the dishwasher mean? | Filling it with dirty plates | *Emptying it and putting the plates away | Mending it | Turning it off
exercise: «Sam unloaded his worries onto his big sister.» What does unloaded mean in this sentence? | Forgot his worries | *Told someone about his worries | Lost his bag | Lifted heavy boxes
test: A lorry arrives at the port full of toys, and the workers unload it. What is the lorry like when they have finished? | *Empty | Full of toys | Painted red | Sinking
test: Maya has 12 boxes and unloads 5 of them. In a maths problem, what do we do with the 5? | Add them | *Subtract them | Multiply them | Round them
exam: Jayden's dad unloads the car, then his sister says, «Now unload your worries.» Which meaning fits the second unload? | Takes things out of a box | Empties a machine | Packs a bag | *Tells someone about his worries
